  "id": "aa13xy5",
  "title": "Chapter 7: Computer Software",
  "order": 7,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "14dbhbr",
      "content": "Computer software refers to a collection of programs, procedures, and related documentation that instructs a computer on how to perform specific tasks. Software acts as an interface between the user and the hardware. Without software, computer hardware cannot function."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Software Types",
          "value": "3 Main Categories",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Focus",
          "value": "System & Application",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Maintenance",
          "value": "Utility Tools",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "uztdvyc"
    },
    {
      "id": "m6r1q0b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Meaning of Computer Software"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computer software is classified primarily into System Software, Application Software, and Utility Software.",
        "System Software manages hardware resources and provides a platform for application programs to run.",
        "Application Software is designed to perform specific user-oriented tasks such as word processing and browser operations.",
        "Utility Software focuses on system maintenance, configuration, optimization, and security management."
      ],
      "id": "v88wmfz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "njzps5z",
      "content": "Software is a set of instructions or programs written using programming languages that tell a computer how to perform tasks. It enables communication between the user and the computer hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "49nhtrc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7.1.1 Characteristics of Software"
    },
    {
      "id": "w505ar1",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Software is intangible – it cannot be physically touched.",
        "It consists of programs and instructions.",
        "It controls the working of hardware.",
        "It can be easily copied and distributed.",
        "It requires updates and maintenance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9mp2iwa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
